  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/eduardofuncao/squix/tarball/v0.5.4-beta",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/eduardofuncao/squix/zipball/v0.5.4-beta",
  "body": "## What's Changed\r\n* feat(build): add negative build flags to compile squix without a set of database drivers by @eduardofuncao in https://github.com/eduardofuncao/squix/pull/91\r\n\r\nOn this and next releases, each squix version will also build the lite and minimal versions for each os/arch combination:\r\n- lite version excludes oracle, snowflake and duckdb drivers, with the bianary size at around ~20mb\r\n- minimal version excludes every driver except for postgres, mysql and sqlite, with the binary size at around ~10mb\r\n\r\nTo build squix excluding any combination of db drivers, use negative tags, for example:\r\n```bash\r\ngo build --tags nopostgres,nosqlite,noduckdb -o squix ./cmd/squix\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo build squix using the nix flake, it is now possible to target lite or minimal version as well\r\n```bash\r\nnix build .#lite\r\n# or\r\nnix build .#minimal\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/eduardofuncao/squix/compare/v0.5.3-beta...v0.5.4-beta",
  "mentions_count": 1
